<title>ARGENTINA: More isolated showers in Argentine grain belt.</title>
<headline>More isolated showers in Argentine grain belt.</headline>
<dateline>BUENOS AIRES 1997-01-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>More isolated showers and storms were set to hit parts of Argentina's main grain areas Tuesday, and traders said it was good for the maize, soybean and sunflower crops.</p>
<p>&quot;Once again, the rain is good as it helps the plants withstand the high temperatures,&quot; one trader said.</p>
<p>The Argentine government's Meteorological Service said there was a possibility of isolated storms and showers in La Pampa, Buenos Aires, Cordoba, Santa Fe, and Entre Rios.</p>
<p>Weather Services Corporation forecast maximum temperatures on grain areas of 88-98F (31-37C).</p>
<p>((--Jason Webb, Buenos Aires Newsroom +541 318-0655))</p>
